            <ArticleTitle>Ask the doctor. After I had and abnormal electrocardiogram,my doctor wants me to have a nuclear stress test to check my arteries for any blockages. (I also have a left side bundle block.) What noninvasive test would give as much information (or almost as much) as a nuclear stress test? I have had many scans, for this and that, so I would like to limit my exposure to radiation if possible.</ArticleTitle>
